#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110297 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110659 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95f11186-e295-5091-93c3-07072b0c18eb" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Power of Quotient Rule with One Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "dc436197-3170-5ed7-a8f8-2092dd72da21" :question/math-academy-id "e-1085" :question/problem "Calculate $\\left(\\dfrac{2x}{3}\\right)^4$." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{2x}{3})^{4} = ((2x)^{4})/(3^{4})\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((2x)^{4})/(3^{4}) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{2^{4}x^{4}}{3^{4}} &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{16x^{4}}{81}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110298 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110660 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "422bde20-bd83-5a20-b708-734b585ac256" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Power of Quotient Rule with Two Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "7d8ea34f-b406-5bc8-9c00-de65d72e9d6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-1086" :question/problem "Simplify $\\left(\\dfrac{y}{2}\\right)^3 \\left(\\dfrac{2y}{3}\\right)^2$." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{y}{2})^{3}(\\frac{2y}{3})^{2} = \\frac{y^{3}}{2^{3}} \\cdot ((2y)^{2})/(3^{2})\n$$\n\nNext, we apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{y^{3}}{2^{3}} \\cdot ((2y)^{2})/(3^{2}) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{y^{3}}{8} \\cdot \\frac{2^{2}y^{2}}{9} &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{y^{3}}{8} \\cdot \\frac{4y^{2}}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the product rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{y^{3}}{8} \\cdot \\frac{4y^{2}}{9} &=  \\\\\n(4y^{(3 + 2)})/(72) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{4y^{5}}{72} &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{y^{5}}{18}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
